    "diff_hunk": "@@ -104627,23 +104669,33 @@ dictionary <dfn>StorageEventInit</dfn> : <span>EventInit</span> {\n   the <span>tokenization</span> stage.</p>\n \n   <p>The <dfn>next input character</dfn> is the first character in the <span>input stream</span>\n-  that has not yet been <dfn data-x=\"\">consumed</dfn> or explicitly ignored by the requirements in\n-  this section. Initially, the <i data-x=\"next input character\">next input character</i> is the\n-  first character in the input. The <dfn>current input character</dfn> is the last character to have\n-  been <i>consumed</i>.</p>\n+  that has not yet been <span data-x=\"consume next input character\">consumed</span> or explicitly\n+  ignored by the requirements in this section. Initially, the <span\n+  data-x=\"next input character\">next input character</span> is the first character in the input.</p>\n+\n+  <p>To <dfn data-x=\"consume next input character\">consume</dfn> the <span>next input\n+  character</span>:</p>\n+\n+  <ol>\n+   <li><p>Let <var>character</var> be the result of <span data-x=\"I/O queue read\">reading</span> one\n+   code point from the <span>input stream</span>.</p></li>\n+\n+   <li><p>If <var>character</var> is to be ignored by the preprocessing rules above, return the\n+   result of <span data-x=\"consume next input character\">consuming</span> the <span>next input\n+   character</span>. Otherwise, if <var>character</var> is to be replaced by the preprocessing rules\n+   above, set <var>character</var> to its replacement.</p></li>\n+\n+   <li><p>Return <var>character</var>. <var>character</var> is now the <dfn>current input\n+   character</dfn>.</p>\n+  </ol>",
