    "body": "As @domenic pointed out to me in #5913, the way the spec is written right now, it's perfectly valid for implementations to use 0 bytes for the prescan and then do anything, up to implementing their own spec-incompatible prescan, in the \"autodetect\" stage. So this change, which prevents that kind of interpretation, is clearly not editorial, though it might be still worth including separately.",
